1. Insertion Variants

Write a program to insert a node before a given value in a singly linked list.

Insert a new node after every even-valued node in a linked list.

Insert a node after every k nodes in a linked list.

Create a linked list from an array of integers dynamically.

Insert a node in a linked list such that the list remains sorted after insertion.

Write a program to insert multiple nodes at once using user input until -1 is entered.

Write a program to insert a node between two nodes if their sum is greater than a given number.

Insert a node at the second last position of a linked list.

Insert nodes at both ends alternatively (front, back, front, back...).

Insert a node into a circular linked list so the list remains sorted.

🗑️ 2. Deletion Variants

Delete all nodes whose data value is greater than a given number.

Delete the second node of every consecutive pair.

Delete the middle node of a linked list (if even, delete second of the two middles).

Delete all nodes having duplicate values completely (not just consecutive).

Delete every kth node from the linked list.

Delete nodes in the linked list having data less than their next node’s data.

Delete nodes having data greater than their next node’s data.

Delete all nodes except the first and last.

Delete all nodes from the linked list that appear more than once.

Delete all nodes in a circular linked list that have odd values.

🔍 3. Searching, Counting & Analysis

Search and return the position of the last occurrence of a given value.

Count the number of prime numbers in a linked list.

Count how many nodes contain palindromic numbers.

Count and print all nodes at even and odd positions separately.

Count the number of nodes before a specific key value.

Count the total number of unique elements in the list.

Search whether the linked list is sorted or not.

Search and display the frequency of each unique element in a linked list.

Write a function to find the nth node from the end.



🔄 4. Modification / Transformation

Replace all negative numbers with 0 in a linked list.

Swap the data of first and last node in the list.

Swap every pair of adjacent nodes.

Rearrange nodes so that all even elements appear before odd ones.

Rearrange nodes so that data in alternate nodes are swapped.

Reverse only the first half of the linked list.

Reverse the linked list in groups of k.

Make a deep copy (clone) of a linked list using pointers.

Split the linked list into two separate lists: one for even values, one for odd values.

Convert a singly linked list to a circular linked list.

🌀 5. Circular Linked List Specific

Create a circular linked list and display elements 3 times (to show looping).

Search whether a given value exists in a circular linked list.

Insert a node after every odd-valued node in a circular linked list.

Delete the head node in a circular linked list and make the next node new head.

Delete the last node of a circular linked list.

Count the number of nodes in a circular linked list without infinite looping.

Find the length of the circular linked list using two pointers.

Split a circular linked list into two equal halves.

Merge two circular linked lists into a single one.

Implement a Circular Doubly Linked List and perform insertion & deletion at both ends.

💥 6. Creative / Exam-Style Challenges

Write a function that deletes every node that has a duplicate immediately before or after it.

Write a function to check if a linked list is palindrome using pointers.

Write a function to rotate a linked list by k nodes (move first k nodes to end).

Write a function to swap k-th node from start and k-th node from end.

Write a function to find intersection point of two linked lists (common node).

Write a program to detect and remove a cycle in a linked list (Floyd’s algorithm).

Write a function to sum two numbers represented by linked lists (e.g., 234 + 789).

Write a function to remove duplicate nodes from an unsorted linked list.

Write a program to compare two linked lists for equality.

Write a program to concatenate two linked lists.